            <div xml:id="d568">

                <pb facs="0752" n="658" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg658"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">871.6363/228: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Rumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Riggs</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-10-04T13:00:00+01:44"><hi rendition="#italic">October 4,
                                1924—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>65. Referring to the Department’s number 34, July 30, 5 p.m., paragraph 7.<anchor
                        n="63" xml:id="d568-f1"/> Have today received confirmation through banks and
                        <pb facs="0753" n="659" xml:id="pg659"/> informed at Ministry Justice of
                    press reports that the Term of Grace Law was extended on the second instant for
                    three months from September 15th, date of its last expiration. Please inform
                    Department of Commerce.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Riggs</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
